<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23652" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεικᾰνάω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δείκνυμι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>point out,
				show,</i> in 
				Ion.
			 and 
				Ep.
			
			impf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεικανάασκεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					24.57
				</span></i>
			; 
				Ep.
			3pl.
			pres.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεικανόωσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arat.
					209
				</span></i>
			: but </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δειδίσκομαι</span>)
				<i>salute, pledge,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεικανόωντο δέπασσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.86
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεικανόωντ᾽ ἐπέεσσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					18.111
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεκανᾶται.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
